  "worked_solution": "First, we convert $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians to an equivalent measure in degrees. This gives\n\n$$\n(\\frac{\\pi }{4})(\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{\\pi })=\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{4}={45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since we know that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1.\n$$",
